      <div type="clause" n="54.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 54.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="54.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="348" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ se ðe hæbbe rihtwif ⁊ eac cifese<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.12-2"/>, ne do him nan preost nan þæra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.13"/> gerihta, þe man Cristenu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> men don sceal<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.14"/>, ærþa<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.15"/></hi> he geswice ⁊ swa deope gebete, swa bisceop<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.16"/> him tæce, ⁊ æfre swylces<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.17"/> geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="54.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="348" ed="#liebermann"/>And se ðe habbe rihtwif ⁊ eac cefese, ne do him nan preost nan ðære rihte, ðe man Cristenu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> men don sceal, ær he geswice ⁊ swa deope gebete, swa him se bisceop tæce, ⁊ æfre swilces geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="54.1" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="348" ed="#liebermann"/>And se ðe hæbbe rihtwif ⁊ eac ceafese, ne do hi<hi rend="italic">m</hi> nan preost nan þara gerihta, þe man Cristenum menn don sceall, ær he geswice ⁊ swa deope gebete, swa biscop him tæce, ⁊ æfre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.1"/> swylces geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="54.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="349" ed="#liebermann"/>Et qui sponsam et concubinam simul habebit, non faciat ei presbiter aliquid rectitudinum, que Christiano pertinent<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.11"/> fieri (debent), priusquam peniteat et ita emendet, sicut episcopus iniunget, et semper deinceps in talibus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.12"/> (super his) abstineat.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="54.1" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="349" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui habet legalem coniugem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.6"/> et etiam concubinam, nullus presbiter nec aliquis alius faciat sibi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.7"/> aliquod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.8"/> seruitium, quod Christiano fieri debet, antequam cessauerit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="54.1" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="349" ed="#liebermann"/>[54, 1] Qui [tamen] simul habuit uxorem et concubinam, nemo presbiter faciat ei rectitudinem quamquam, que Christiano fieri debeat, donec cessauerit et delictum correxerit, sicut ei episcopus iniunxerit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="54.1" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="202" ed="#robertson"/>And se ðe habbe rihtwif ⁊ eac cefese, ne do him nan preost nan ðære rihte<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#IICn_54-1.robnote.fn.9"/> ðe man Cristenum men don sceal, ær he geswice ⁊ swa deope gebete swa him se<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_54-1.robnote.fn.3"/> bisceop tæce, ⁊ æfre swilces geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="282" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And se ðe hæbbe rihtwif and eac cifese, ne do him nan preost nan þæra gerihta þe man Cristenum men don sceal, ær þam he geswice and swa deope gebete swa bisceop him tæce, and æfre swylces geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="348" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.de.1"/> eine <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.de1.star"/>Ehefrau<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.de.2"/> und daneben ein Kebsweib<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.de.3"/> hat, dem leiste kein Priester einen jener [Seelenheil-]Dienste, die <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.de1.star-2"/>man dem Christenmenschen zu <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.de1.star-3"/>leisten schuldet, bevor jener [von Concubinat] abstehe und so tief büsse, wie der Bischof ihm vorschreibt, und künftig von solchem abstehen will.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_54-1.lnote.de.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And whoever has a wife and besides her a concubine, let no priest perform for him any of those [soul's-health] services which one owes to perform for a Christian man, before he desists [from concubinage] and atones as deeply as the bishop prescribes to him, and is willing in future to desist from such.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_54-1.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="203" ed="#robertson"/>And if anyone has a lawful wife and also a concubine, no priest shall perform for him any of the offices which must be performed for a Christian man, until he desists and makes amends as thoroughly as the bishop shall direct him, and ever afterwards desists from such [evildoing].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="470" ed="#whitelock"/>And if anyone has a lawful wife and also a concubine, no priest is to do for him any of the offices which must be done for a Christian man, until he desists and atones for it as deeply as the bishop directs him, and desists from such for ever.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="283" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if anyone has a legal wife as well as a mistress, no priest shall perform for him any of the sacraments to which a Christian is entitled until he ceases and repents as profoundly as the bishop instructs, and afterward entirely abstains from such sins.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="348">Poen. Ps. Theod. 19, 33; Can. Edg., Mo. poen. 17; Poen. Egb. II 9</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">*(Poen. Ps. Theod. 19, 33;) Can. Edg., Mo. poen. 17; Poen. Egb. II 9</note>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 349, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">bisceop him: him se bisceop B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cum <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cum Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">faciant eis <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">faciant eis Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verb. aus</hi> tempus <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from tempus Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">p. f. <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> f. d. <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">p. f. K; f. d. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">in t. <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> s. h. <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in t. K; s. h. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.12-2" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ceaf. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ceaf. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðara <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðara Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sceall <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sceall Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ær <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ær Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-cop <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-cop Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">swil. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">swil. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verb. aus</hi> afre</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from afre</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr. H</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above H</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ei <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ei Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-quid <hi rend="italic">DiLbS</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-quid DiLbS</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Teils Eadgar, teils Ps.-Egbert näher</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Closer partly to Eadgar, partly to Ps.-Egbert</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.de1.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">(<hi rend="italic">Poen. Ps. Theod.</hi> 19, 33;) <hi rend="italic">Can. Edg., Mo. poen.</hi> 17; <hi rend="italic">Poen. Egb. II</hi> 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">(<hi rend="italic">Poen. Ps. Theod.</hi> 19, 33;) <hi rend="italic">Can. Edg., Mo. poen.</hi> 17; <hi rend="italic">Poen. Egb. II</hi> 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Kompositum <hi rend="italic">rihtwif</hi> (in Einem Wort Hs. B) fehlt Toller; aber <hi rend="italic">s. o</hi>. 53³; <hi rend="italic">rihtæwe</hi> Egb.; <hi rend="italic">æwe</hi> Edg.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The compound <hi rend="italic">rihtwif</hi> (as one word in MS B) is missing in Toller; but <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> 53³; <hi rend="italic">rihtæwe</hi> Egb.; <hi rend="italic">æwe</hi> Edg.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Konkubinat 6b. Auch Ps.-Theodor 19,33: <hi rend="italic">Qui uxorem simul habet et concubinam non communicet</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Konkubinat 6b. Also Ps.-Theodore 19,33: <hi rend="italic">Qui uxorem simul habet et concubinam non communicet</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.de1.star-2" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">(<hi rend="italic">Poen. Ps. Theod.</hi> 19, 33;) <hi rend="italic">Can. Edg., Mo. poen.</hi> 17; <hi rend="italic">Poen. Egb. II</hi> 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">(<hi rend="italic">Poen. Ps. Theod.</hi> 19, 33;) <hi rend="italic">Can. Edg., Mo. poen.</hi> 17; <hi rend="italic">Poen. Egb. II</hi> 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.de1.star-3" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">(<hi rend="italic">Poen. Ps. Theod.</hi> 19, 33;) <hi rend="italic">Can. Edg., Mo. poen.</hi> 17; <hi rend="italic">Poen. Egb. II</hi> 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">(<hi rend="italic">Poen. Ps. Theod.</hi> 19, 33;) <hi rend="italic">Can. Edg., Mo. poen.</hi> 17; <hi rend="italic">Poen. Egb. II</hi> 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_54-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Lateiner übersetzen nur Ein <hi rend="italic">geswice</hi>; das zweite ist aber eine Erweiterung; es betrifft durch <hi rend="italic">æfre</hi> auch die Zukunft</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The Latin translators render only one <hi rend="italic">geswice</hi>; the second, however, is an extension; through <hi rend="italic">æfre</hi> it also concerns the future</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_54-1.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. <hi rend="italic">Can. Edg.</hi>, <hi rend="italic">Mod. poenit.</hi> 17, <hi rend="italic">ibid.</hi> p. 270; <hi rend="italic">Poen. Egb.</hi> <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi>. 9, <hi rend="italic">ibid.</hi> pp. 184, 186; <hi rend="italic">Poen. Theod.</hi> 19 § 33, <hi rend="italic">ibid.</hi> p. 20.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_54-1.robnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">202</biblScope></bibl><label>his</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_54-1.robnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">202</biblScope></bibl><label>rihte</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þæra</hi> (<hi rend="italic">þara, ðara</hi>) <hi rend="italic">gerihta</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
